data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `nint` and `nuint` into a `Span`.**

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

Both work without requiring `unsafe` context (since the result is assigned to a `Span<T>`). On this 64-bit system, each element is 8 bytes. The only quirk is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an unsafe context (or use `Unsafe.SizeOf<nint>()`) because the size isn't known at compile time — but `stackalloc` itself has no such restriction.
